    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0468" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg394"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Pike</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 241.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 3,1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatch of the 17th
                    ultimo, No. 166, together with a copy of a note which you addressed to the
                    minister of foreign affairs on the reception of the news of the surrender of the
                    remaining military forces of the insurgents, and it is fully approved by this
                    department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Pike,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
